    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" id="tutorial-2d">
  <div class="panel-head"><div class="panel-title">Tutorial: a playable 2D platformer</div></div>
  <div class="panel-body doc">
    <p>The fastest route is the <strong>2D Platformer</strong> template. Build one from scratch with these steps:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Create a 2D game. Select the starter scene and delete extra objects, keeping a ground object.</li>
      <li>Add <strong>Sprite</strong> objects for the player and platforms. Give the player a SpriteRenderer, Rigidbody2D (dynamic) and Collider2D. Platforms get a static Rigidbody2D and a Collider2D.</li>
      <li>Add a <strong>Camera2D</strong>. In the Inspector set follow/target to the player if the component exposes it, or move the camera with a script.</li>
      <li>Create a visual script named <em>Player</em>. Add an <strong>On Update</strong> node and an <strong>Input Axis</strong> node with action <span class="code">horizontal</span>.</li>
      <li>Add a <strong>Set Velocity</strong> action for the player. Connect On Update → Set Velocity, then Input Axis.value → Set Velocity.x. Type a speed value (for example <span class="code">180</span>) into the remaining input.</li>
      <li>Add <strong>Key Pressed</strong> for <span class="code">Space</span>, a branch, and an <strong>Apply Impulse</strong> action. Connect the jump branch to the impulse and set the Y impulse.</li>
      <li>Press <strong>Play</strong>. Tune gravity in Project settings and the impulse value in the node Inspector; changes autosave.</li>
      <li>Compile, fix any Problems, then export standalone HTML or publish.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="hint">Exact node names come from the node library; use the search box and read each node's description before connecting.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" id="tutorial-3d">
  <div class="panel-head"><div class="panel-title">Tutorial: a 3D first-person scene</div></div>
  <div class="panel-body doc">
    <ol>
      <li>Create a 3D game or start from <strong>First-Person Vault</strong>. The template includes a character controller, imported crate, door interaction, HUD and win condition.</li>
      <li>Scene: a ground plane/cube, walls, a light, and a camera at eye height. Set the camera's Camera3D component and attach the character controller to the player object.</li>
      <li>Move with WASD and look with the mouse in Play mode. Physics uses Cannon-es; collisions need a Collider3D and Rigidbody3D.</li>
      <li>Interaction: add a visual script with <strong>On Key Pressed</strong> (<span class="code">KeyE</span>), a <strong>Raycast</strong>/proximity check if available, and an action that opens the door or sets a win variable.</li>
      <li>UI: add UIElement components for a crosshair and objective text, bind them to project variables in the Inspector.</li>
      <li>Play, then Compile and publish. The exported HTML includes Three.js and Cannon-es, so it runs offline.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="hint">If WebGL is unavailable the 3D viewport may render blank; the 2D editor and exports still work. Use a hardware-accelerated browser for 3D.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" id="troubleshooting">
  <div class="panel-head"><div class="panel-title">Troubleshooting &amp; current limits</div></div>
  <div class="panel-body doc">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Nothing moves in Play</strong> — check the script trigger (On Update vs On Game Start), the script's attached object, and that the body is dynamic.</li>
      <li><strong>A node will not connect</strong> — exec pins connect only to exec pins; data types must match or one side must be <span class="code">any</span>/<span class="code">json</span>. Type a literal instead, or add a conversion node.</li>
      <li><strong>Export says "Build failed"</strong> — open Problems. Compilation must pass; exports never ship a broken graph.</li>
      <li><strong>An object cannot be clicked</strong> — it is locked or hidden. Select it in the Hierarchy; the padlock/eye buttons toggle both.</li>
      <li><strong>Large HTML export</strong> — models and audio are inlined. Use ZIP export or smaller assets.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Not implemented yet:</strong> navigation/behavior trees, skeletal animation playback/blending/state machines, networked 3D multiplayer, mesh editing/sculpting, advanced post-processing and terrain sculpting/painting/chunks/LOD. Terrain is a procedural heightfield with a simple collider. Imported animations are not played by the runtime.</p>
  </div>
</section>

